        "sender_full_name": "Iván Renison",
        "timestamp": 1775087076
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"646655\">Iván Renison</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/List.2EnotMem_subset/near/583151473\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Would <code>List.notMem_subset</code> be welcome to Mathlib, or is there a reason not to have it?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Maybe more suited for <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries\">batteries</a>? Though it does use set so maybe not.</p>",
